{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["כי מראש צרים אראנו — that I, standing now, see them. He explains the reason why the Holy One, blessed be He, did not become angry with them and why He has no desire to curse them: for — from the top of the rocks — I, standing now, see them, and from the top of the hill I behold them, for they are alone by themselves and no other nations are reckoned among them or intermingled with them, and also they have small children who are not counted, for they were counted only from twenty years old and upward; they are therefore far more numerous [than they appear]. For —"], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The comment ends with כי - introducing the next scriptural phrase, left dangling as Rashbam proceeds to expound it."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:50:49.077855811Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}